    "title": "The Grasshopper — NZ forecast",
    "summary": "The weather really let rip over the weekend, with severe gales keeping most ski fields closed and limiting lift operations at the few that managed to open. However, a cold change swept through on Sunday, delivering 5-20cm of wind-blown powder to the Southern Lakes and a 2-5cm dusting to Canterbury, with more falling through the day. Mt Ruapehu also scored some fresh snow, mainly on the upper slopes.",
