      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona 24 Aug 2026 – It's a powder day at Cardrona after 26cm of wind-affected snow landed over the last 48 hours. The morning is clear with moderate westerly winds, temperatures sitting around 0°C, and the team is still working through some overnight wind damage — expect possible delays as crews dig out the base area and get terrain opening. Wind holds are possible through the day, so keep an eye on lift status if you're heading up top. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express and the T-Bar are running, giving access to Learners Slope, Main Basin, Captains, Ski Touring Access and Summit. Soho Express and Willow's Quad remain on wind hold, so Soho, Little Willows and Big Willows are unavailable for now, with staff aiming to bring them online through the morning. Wells Pipe Platter is closed for the day, and Mt Cardrona is also closed. In the park, Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley and Stag Lane are open, while Big Bucks sits on hold and the Half-Pipe is closed today. The access road is chain-free but chains must still be carried, and there's an active hazard advisory worth checking before you drive up — Carparks A and B are already full, with space still available at C, the Yard, Valley View and the Pines.",
