      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 24 Aug 2026 – The wind has eased right off and it's a cracker up here, with sunshine, calm conditions and plenty of wind-loaded stashes scattered across the mountain. Sitting around 1°C with light westerlies for now, today's shaping up as one of the better days of the week — an afternoon session is well worth it if you can't make it up early. All three lifts are spinning — Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter — with every groomed run open today, including Triple Treat, Main Street, High Street, Bullet, Saddle Track, Pete's Treat, Raffils Run and Upper Skite. Home Basin, Saddle Basin and Matukituki Basin are all open and skiing well, along with Powder Bowl and Summit Slopes. Motatapu Chutes and Hollywood Bowl are closed today due to poor conditions — riders are reminded that ducking those closures means losing your pass, so respect the signage. The upper car parks are already full, with overflow parking down the road at Pub Corner — carpool or grab the free shuttle if you can. Chains must be carried by all vehicles, and there's an active hazard advisory on the access road worth checking before you head up. The View is open at the base serving pizzas, hot chips and drinks for a well-earned refuel.",
